What are the highest, lowest, and average systolic and diastolic blood pressure readings by doctor. using the average systolic and diastolic readings, which doctor(s) appear to be most successful at managing blood pressure in patients with hypertension

-- Doctor: Ayala, Demi appears to be most successful at managing blood pressure in patients with hypertension

select max(bp.systolic)'Highest Systolic', max(bp.diastolic)'Highest Diastolic',
min(bp.systolic)'Lowest Systolic', min(bp.diastolic)'Lowest Diastolic', 
avg(bp.systolic)'Average Systolic', avg(bp.diastolic)'Average Diastolic',
d.LastName+ ', ' +d.FirstName'Doctor Name'
from encounters e 
join doctors d on d.DoctorID = e.DoctorID
join ##validbp bp on bp.encounterid = e.encounterid 
group by d.LastName+ ', ' +d.FirstName
order by avg(bp.systolic), avg(bp.diastolic)


What are the highest, lowest, and average systolic and diastolic blood pressure readings by facility using the average sytolic and diastolic readings, which facility appears to be most successful at managing blood pressure in patients with hypertension? 

-- "Rest for the Weary" appears to be most successful at managing blood pressure in patiens with hypertension 

select max(bp.systolic)'Highest Systolic', max(bp.diastolic)'Highest Diastolic', min(bp.systolic)'Lowest Systolic', min(bp.diastolic)'Lowest Diastolic', 
avg(bp.systolic)'Average Systolic', avg(bp.diastolic)'Average Diastolic', f.name'Facility Name'
from encounters e
join facilities f on f.facilityid = e.facilityid 
join ##validbp bp on bp.encounterid = e.encounterid 
group by f.name 
order by avg(bp.systolic), avg(bp.diastolic)

What are the highest, lowest, and average systolic and diastolic blood pressure readings by medication. Using the average systolic and diastolic readings, which medications appear to be most succesful at managing blood pressure in patients with hypertension?

select m.MedName'Prescription', max(bp.systolic) 'Highest Systolic', max(bp.diastolic)'Highest Diastolic',
min(bp.systolic) 'Lowest Systolic', min(bp.diastolic) 'Lowest Diastolic',
avg(bp.systolic) 'Average Systolic', avg(bp.diastolic) 'Average Diastolic'
from ##validbp bp
join encounters e on bp.encounterid= e.encounterid
join medications m on e.patientid=m.patientid
where m.bpmed='Y'
group by m.medname
order by avg(bp.systolic), avg(bp.diastolic)


